You are a senior frontend architect and UX auditor. I'm redesigning the UI/UX of
our customer interaction portal and need a complete, factual audit of the CURRENT
frontend so a world-class UI/UX designer can redesign it without seeing the code.

RULES
- Do NOT modify any code. Read-only analysis.
- Do NOT guess or invent. If something can't be determined from the code, write "UNKNOWN".
- Be specific: use real file paths, component names, route names, and actual values.
- Output ONE markdown document using exactly the sections below.

---
## 0. PRODUCT & DOMAIN CONTEXT (infer from README, docs, models, API names, copy, comments)
- What this portal is for, in plain language (2-3 sentences)
- The business domain/industry it serves
- Core entities/objects in the system (e.g. Customer, Ticket, Order, Invoice, Project)
  and how they relate to each other
- Main features/modules and what each does
- Main user journeys, from the user's goal to the outcome
- Integrations (CRM, payment, email/SMS, WhatsApp, third-party APIs)
- Any terminology/jargon the UI uses that a new user might not understand
- Anything in the code, docs, or comments that hints at business rules,
  SLAs, statuses/workflows (e.g. Open → In Progress → Resolved), or permissions
Mark anything you can't confirm as "UNKNOWN".

## 1. TECH STACK
- Framework + version (React/Next/Vue/Angular/etc.), language (JS/TS)
- Styling approach (Tailwind, CSS modules, styled-components, SCSS, plain CSS, mixed?)
- UI library, if any (MUI, AntD, Bootstrap, shadcn, Chakra...) + version
- State management, routing, form library, data fetching, i18n, charting libs
- Build tool, and any CSS/JS conventions or linters enforced

## 2. PROJECT STRUCTURE
- Folder tree (top 3 levels) for the frontend
- Where pages, components, styles, assets, and API calls live

## 3. SITEMAP / ROUTES
For EVERY route/page, give a table:
| Route | Page/file | Purpose | Auth required? | Roles allowed |

## 4. USER ROLES & FLOWS
- All user roles in the system (customer, agent, admin, etc.) and what each can see/do
- Step-by-step main flows as implemented (e.g. login → dashboard → raise ticket →
  chat → track status). List the screens and actions in order.

## 5. PAGE-BY-PAGE BREAKDOWN
For EACH page/screen:
- Purpose and what the user is trying to achieve
- Layout structure (header, sidebar, tabs, cards, tables, modals, etc.)
- Every component used on it
- Every data field shown (labels, types, example values)
- Every action available (buttons, links, forms, filters, search, sort, pagination, bulk actions)
- Empty, loading, error, and success states (are they handled? how?)
- API endpoints it calls (method, path, request/response shape)

## 6. COMPONENT INVENTORY
- List all reusable components: name, path, props, where used, and variants
- Flag duplicates / near-duplicates / inconsistent versions of the same thing
  (e.g. 4 different button styles)

## 7. CURRENT DESIGN SYSTEM (AS-IS)
- Colors: every hex/rgb/CSS variable actually in use, grouped by usage
  (primary, text, background, borders, status colors) + count of one-off hardcoded colors
- Typography: font families, sizes, weights, line-heights actually used
- Spacing, border radius, shadows, breakpoints
- Icons (library or custom), logos, images, brand assets and their file paths
- Dark mode support? Theming setup?

## 8. FORMS & INTERACTIONS
- Every form: fields, input types, validation rules, error messages, submit behavior
- Modals, drawers, toasts, tooltips, confirmations
- Real-time features (chat, notifications, websockets, polling)
- File uploads, attachments, downloads

## 9. RESPONSIVENESS & ACCESSIBILITY
- How responsive is it? Which breakpoints exist? Which pages break on mobile?
- Accessibility problems you can detect: missing alt/labels, contrast issues,
  keyboard navigation, focus states, ARIA misuse, semantic HTML problems

## 10. PERFORMANCE & TECHNICAL DEBT
- Heavy components/pages, unnecessary re-renders, large bundles, unoptimized images
- Inline styles, !important usage, dead CSS, copy-pasted code, inconsistent patterns
- Anything that would make a UI redesign hard (tight coupling of logic and markup,
  global CSS collisions, etc.)

## 11. UX PROBLEMS YOU CAN SPOT FROM THE CODE
List concrete issues: confusing navigation, too many steps, unclear labels,
inconsistent patterns, missing feedback, cluttered screens, missing states.
For each: where it is + why it's a problem.

## 12. CONSTRAINTS
- What must NOT change (API contracts, auth flow, required fields, legal text, integrations)
- Third-party widgets/embeds (payment, chat, analytics, maps)
- Browser support requirements, if any are configured

## 13. KEY CODE SAMPLES
Paste the full code of: (a) the main layout/shell component, (b) the dashboard or
home page, (c) one representative form, (d) one representative table/list,
(e) the global stylesheet / theme / tailwind config.

## 14. SCREENSHOT CHECKLIST
List every page/state I should screenshot for the designer (e.g. login, dashboard,
ticket list, ticket detail, empty state, error state, mobile views).
